      "seed": 2104757066,
      "version": 2146,
      "versionNonce": 363827613,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776015777913,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Streaming Window Types\n\n\nSliding Windows\n\n→ Window = [T - 1 hour, T] — always anchored to right now\n→ Continuously moves forward with time\n→ Example: at 10:06 → window is 9:06 → 10:06\n→ Always reflects the true last 60 minutes of activity\n\n\nTumbling Windows\n\n→ Window = last complete hour bounded by hour boundaries\n→ [Floor(T - 1hr, 'hour'), Floor(T, 'hour')]\n→ Example: at 10:06 → window is 9:00 → 10:00\n→ Fixed, non-overlapping buckets — window only advances when the next boundary is\ncrossed\n\n\nTradeoff:\n\nSliding windows give more accurate real-time signals but are more expensive to compute\n— every event must be continuously re-evaluated as the window moves. Tumbling\nwindows are cheaper and simpler (pre-aggregate per bucket) but introduce up to one full\nwindow of lag — at 10:06, you're still looking at data that's potentially 66 minutes old ⚖️",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "drsrvDXe_9StgowHKlSNW",
      "originalText": "Streaming Window Types\n\n\nSliding Windows\n\n→ Window = [T - 1 hour, T] — always anchored to right now\n→ Continuously moves forward with time\n→ Example: at 10:06 → window is 9:06 → 10:06\n→ Always reflects the true last 60 minutes of activity\n\n\nTumbling Windows\n\n→ Window = last complete hour bounded by hour boundaries\n→ [Floor(T - 1hr, 'hour'), Floor(T, 'hour')]\n→ Example: at 10:06 → window is 9:00 → 10:00\n→ Fixed, non-overlapping buckets — window only advances when the next boundary is crossed\n\n\nTradeoff:\n\nSliding windows give more accurate real-time signals but are more expensive to compute — every event must be continuously re-evaluated as the window moves. Tumbling windows are cheaper and simpler (pre-aggregate per bucket) but introduce up to one full window of lag — at 10:06, you're still looking at data that's potentially 66 minutes old ⚖️",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
