    },
    {
      "id": "1nJiQbNCdrT2Rm6IhXomK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3370.589184560246,
      "y": 252.98566924280266,
      "width": 807.19921875,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1077710067,
      "version": 3141,
      "versionNonce": 1899739837,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776015777913,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scoping the Time Period Requirements\n\n\nArbitrary Time Periods (Below the Line ❌)\n\n→ e.g. \"top K videos for June 2024\"\n→ Would require full general time series query support\n→ Pre-computation becomes largely impossible\n→ Rarely what interviewers are after — don't design for this\n\n\nWhat We're Supporting Instead ✅\n\n→ Fixed, well-known time windows (e.g. last 1hr, last 24hrs, last 7 days)\n→ Allows aggressive pre-computation and caching of results\n→ Massively simplifies the system\n\n\nTradeoff:\nSupporting arbitrary time ranges gives maximum query flexibility but kills your ability to\nprecompute anything — you trade simplicity and performance for generality that's almost\nnever needed in this context ⚖️",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "ZnPk3xuK7langGW2sG1G5",
      "originalText": "Scoping the Time Period Requirements\n\n\nArbitrary Time Periods (Below the Line ❌)\n\n→ e.g. \"top K videos for June 2024\"\n→ Would require full general time series query support\n→ Pre-computation becomes largely impossible\n→ Rarely what interviewers are after — don't design for this\n\n\nWhat We're Supporting Instead ✅\n\n→ Fixed, well-known time windows (e.g. last 1hr, last 24hrs, last 7 days)\n→ Allows aggressive pre-computation and caching of results\n→ Massively simplifies the system\n\n\nTradeoff:\nSupporting arbitrary time ranges gives maximum query flexibility but kills your ability to precompute anything — you trade simplicity and performance for generality that's almost never needed in this context ⚖️",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
