      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776039062958,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Constraining the Size of Top K\n\n→ Result sets must never grow unbounded — always place practical limits on clients\n→ K ≤ 1000 is a reasonable upper bound for almost all top-K use cases\n→ If a client needs top 1M videos, they're effectively asking for the full dataset — that's a\ndifferent problem, served by a different system\n\n\nTradeoff:\nCapping K simplifies storage, computation, and response sizes significantly — the cost is\nthat clients needing very large result sets must use a separate data export/query system\ninstead, but this is the correct separation of concerns ⚖️",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "oIG-zvwpIpaRdCG2U-QDh",
      "originalText": "Constraining the Size of Top K\n\n→ Result sets must never grow unbounded — always place practical limits on clients\n→ K ≤ 1000 is a reasonable upper bound for almost all top-K use cases\n→ If a client needs top 1M videos, they're effectively asking for the full dataset — that's a different problem, served by a different system\n\n\nTradeoff:\nCapping K simplifies storage, computation, and response sizes significantly — the cost is that clients needing very large result sets must use a separate data export/query system instead, but this is the correct separation of concerns ⚖️",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
